sizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 15855, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beach House", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Cigarettes After Sex", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "David Guetta", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Depeche Mode", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "dk", "country_name": "Denmark", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 12453, "best_position": 74}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Calvin Harris", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chappell Roan", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "David Guetta", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Justin Timberlake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "dk", "country_name": "Denmark", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Artigeardit", "streams": 74563, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "KESI", "streams": 49425, "best_position": 11}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 17511, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 15855, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Gilli", "streams": 11408, "best_position": 94}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Black Eyed Peas", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "new wave": {"genre": "new wave", "country_code": "dk", "country_name": "Denmark", "summary": "New wave is today a quite broad umbrella term describing popular music from around 1977 to 1986. But originally it was a slim sub genre of Western popular music that arose in the United Kingdom about 1977-78. It had close ties to punk rock and fairly strong influences of the musical style that had been invented and continuously developed throughout the 1970s: reggae.\n\nThe term new wave was first a kind of description of a more musical and lyric wise complex music than punk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "David Bowie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Depeche Mode", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Fontaines D.C.", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Paramore", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Killers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "nu metal": {"genre": "nu metal", "country_code": "dk", "country_name": "Denmark", "summary": "Nu metal is a subgenre of alternative metal that blends elements of heavy metal with influences from other genres such as hip hop, funk, industrial, and grunge. It typically emphasises rhythm and syncopation, with guitar work often involving down-tuned seven-string guitars to create a heavier sound. Guitar solos and technical displays are generally less common in nu metal. Vocal styles vary and may include singing, rapping, screaming, and occasionally growling.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Slipknot", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "dk", "country_name": "Denmark", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": 17929, "best_position": 45}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 17511, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 15855, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": 13071, "best_position": 65}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 12453, "best_position": 74}, {"artist": "Malcolm Todd", "streams": 12080, "best_position": 84}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ABBA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beach House", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "dk", "country_name": "Denmark", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented w